  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) The paper proposes to develop and evaluate a dimension-dependent design guideline for efficient CPL emitters by tuning oxygen-bearing chiral organic cations that coordinate with K⁺ ions to construct indium-based metal-halide hybrids of increasing dimensionality, thereby investigating chirality transfer, balancing electric and magnetic transition dipole moments, and pursuing simultaneously high photoluminescence quantum yield and a large circularly polarized luminescence dissymmetry factor.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
